* EE463 60 W sync buck - Step 4: input reverse-polarity protection (optional add-on 1), ngspice cross-check
* Q3 (BSC030N08NS5): drain -> VIN- terminal, source -> circuit ground,
* gate -> VIN+ through R1 (100 k), D1 12 V Zener gate clamp (BZT52B12). Bypass footprint JP1 (0 ohm) not fitted.
* The converter is represented by its input capacitors and an equivalent 60 W load at 48 V (37 ohm).
* VIN = +48 V (normal) or -48 V (reversed); change .param VIN.
.param VIN=48

V1    vpos_s vneg_t {VIN}
Rsrc  vpos_s vpos 30m
* reverse-polarity MOSFET Q3 and its gate drive
MQ3   vneg_t g 0 BSC030
R1    vpos g 100k
D1    0 g DZ12
* converter input: C2-C5, C11, C12 (6 x 2.2 uF ceramic at DC bias), C1 100 uF electrolytic, equivalent load
C2_12 vpos 0 6u
C1    vpos nel 100u
Rel   nel 0 0.2
Rconv vpos 0 37

.model DZ12 D(Is=1e-12 N=1 BV=12 IBV=5m Rs=5)
.model BSC030 VDMOS(Rg=1.6 Rd=2.4m Rs=0.3m Vto=3.0 Kp=250 Lambda=0.01
+ Cgdmax=1.4n Cgdmin=40p a=0.5 Cgs=4n Cjo=5n Vj=0.7 M=0.5 Is=1e-12 N=1.05 Rb=1.5m TT=10n BV=80)

.tran 1u 3m
.control
run
meas tran vds AVG v(vneg_t) from=2.5m to=3m
meas tran vgs AVG v(g) from=2.5m to=3m
.endc
.end
